  "passage": "In the nurse's office, there was a blue chair beside the window. Students sat there when they had headaches, stomachaches, or simply needed a quiet moment.\nOne day, the chair broke. The nurse planned to throw it away. But students asked her not to.\nThey wrote notes about the chair. One said, \"I sat here when I cried after a fight.\" Another said, \"This chair helped me calm down before my speech.\"\nThe nurse was surprised. To her, it was just old furniture. To students, it was a safe place.\nThe school repaired the chair and kept it by the window. Sometimes an object becomes important because of the feelings people leave there.",
